Package: RMTIF
Type: Package
Title: Restricted Mean Time in Favor of Treatment
Version: 0.3.1
Authors@R: person("Mohsen", "Rezapour", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "mrezapou@amgen.com")
Description: Estimates restricted mean time in favor of treatment from ordered
    multistate trajectories, with lower states denoting better outcomes.
    Provides complete-path pairwise estimation, projection standard errors,
    normal confidence intervals and tests, terminal-aware inverse probability
    of censoring weighting, stratified bootstrap inference, and pairwise
    regression with sandwich or refitted-bootstrap inference. Includes
    parameterized simulation and Monte Carlo summary tools for reversible
    processes, continuous-time Markov paths, constant-utility regression,
    and comparisons of longitudinal oncology endpoints.
    The restricted-time estimand follows Mao (2023)
    <doi:10.1111/biom.13570>; pairwise regression is motivated by the
    proportional win-fractions framework of Mao and Wang (2021)
    <doi:10.1111/biom.13382>.
